      "attempt_id": "B_transitive_attempt_1",
      "message": ".\n- `consume(old, new)` (the required entry point) \u2014 returns a dict:\n  - `allowed` = `can_transition(old, new)`\n  - `status` = `\"accepted\"` / `\"rejected\"`, plus a `reason` string on rejection\n  - echoes `old`, `new`, and `contract_version` so callers can see which semantics were frozen in.\n- Module `__main__` self-check exercising the two allowed and four rejected pairs.\n\n### Preserved assumption (documented in the module docstring)\nOnly `('new','paid')` and `('new','cancelled')` are legal; everything else is rejected. The docstring explicitly warns that a future contract v2 must be re-synced manually rather than picked up at runtime \u2014 this fork pins v1 behavior deliberately and will silently keep enforcing v1 otherwise.\n\n### Verification\n`consume('new','paid')` \u2192 allowed/accepted; `consume('new','cancelled')` \u2192 allowed/accepted; `consume('paid','cancelled')` \u2192 rejected; `consume('new','new')` \u2192 rejected. Confirmed the source contains no `import semkg_contract` / `from semkg_contract`."
