      "attempt_id": "B_transitive_attempt_2",
      "message": "{('new','paid'), ('new','cancelled'), ('paid','refunded')})` \u2014 exactly the membership set the contract's `can_transition` uses.\n  - `KNOWN_STATES` derived from that table (`new`, `paid`, `cancelled`, `refunded`); `TERMINAL_STATES = {'refunded','cancelled'}` (no outgoing edges in v2).\n- `can_transition(old, new)` \u2014 reproduced contract check: `(old, new) in ALLOWED_TRANSITIONS` (rejects unknown states, self-transitions, and reversed/illegal pairs such as `paid->cancelled`, `new->refunded`, `refunded->paid`).\n- **`consume(old, new)`** \u2014 pure, no I/O; returns a dict with `contract_version`, `old`, `new`, `allowed`, `reason` (`allowed by contract v2` / `unknown_state: ...` / `illegal_transition: ...`), `next_state` (adopts `new` only if allowed, else retains `old`), and `terminal` (whether `next_state` is terminal).\n- `consume_batch(transitions)` \u2014 convenience helper threading `next_state` across a lifecycle chain.\n\nNo other files were created or modified; no repository-wide tests were run."
